{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793846693,"nonce":"+OfYFiJGdSru/pdXkVGt0eJl8Mo=","title":"Hot interpreted calls compile synchronously when compile workers are saturated","message":"An unqueued call at or above the baseline threshold falls back to osr::try_lazy_compile on its execution thread whenever existing workers are all busy. This is distinct from having no workers: execution should continue interpreted and queue demand for the existing worker pool. Keep no-worker fallback, deduplicate repeated demand, retain stale-request checks, and stop accepting work after shutdown. This is the bounded fix extracted from the broader scheduling investigation in 96f11d1; the OSR concurrency/static-hot changes there regressed benchmarks and are not part of this fix.","files":null}]}